abstract: >-
  A small, citable, dependency-free Python package for linear (Airy) and Stokes
  water-wave theory. It solves the dispersion relation, reproduces the
  University of Delaware / CACR wave-calculator output set (wavelength,
  wavenumber, celerity, group velocity, direction, shoaling and refraction
  coefficients, and bottom orbital velocity), provides closed-form Airy and
  second-order Stokes surface elevation, and exposes the Ursell number (two
  pinned conventions) with a transparent wave-theory applicability gate. It
  additionally answers the Lagrangian question that Eulerian wave calculators do
  not: the closed-form Stokes drift profile, the depth-integrated Stokes
  transport, a single mean drift velocity directly comparable to the net
  velocity a GNSS-tracked drifter reports, and an RK4 particle integrator whose
  net parcel velocity converges to the closed form as wave steepness vanishes. A
  raschii bridge supplies higher-order Stokes and Fenton stream-function
  profiles.
